WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.887
Step three runs the inventory
against the fictional estate.

2
00:00:03.887 --> 00:00:08.299
It reads thirty-five identities,
fifteen from Active Directory and

3
00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:12.788
twenty from Entra, and rates eight
high, eight medium and nineteen low.

4
00:00:12.788 --> 00:00:16.782
That's eight findings, eleven
warnings and three information items,

5
00:00:16.782 --> 00:00:19.849
and three accounts handed
to the Data Platform plan.

6
00:00:19.849 --> 00:00:24.938
The manifest records the tenant, every
request, and a hash of every file.

7
00:00:24.938 --> 00:00:27.913
Step four reads the eight
high-risk identities.

8
00:00:27.913 --> 00:00:32.523
Three accounts have passwords that
never expire, and one of them,

9
00:00:32.523 --> 00:00:36.351
svc oldftp, is also a stale
lead, so verify its use first.

10
00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:39.994
j doe was found only by a
password that never expires,

11
00:00:39.994 --> 00:00:42.875
so it may be a person,
not a service account.

12
00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:45.997
Others sit in Backup
Operators or Domain Admins,

13
00:00:45.997 --> 00:00:48.963
or are trusted for
unconstrained delegation.

14
00:00:48.963 --> 00:00:52.800
And the Mail Automation app holds
a directory-wide write permission.
